From 33bcfb2ecb0e8cc062e670aa717a9ead9732afbb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Mingyang Sun (Public)" <mingsun@amd.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 22:30:14 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 15/16] fix(clr): separate the pk8 scale gating from the pk16
 gating

Review feedback (@mangupta): a single HIP_ENABLE_GFX1250_BLOCK16_BUILTINS
predicate currently covers two decisions of very different confidence, so
the uncertain one cannot be reverted without disturbing the correct one.

The pk16 gating is correct regardless of how LCOMPILER-2841 resolves:
MI450-A0's V_CVT_SCALE_PK32_*_{FP6,BF6} opcodes 674-679 were replaced in
B0 by V_CVT_SCALE_PK16_* at 711-716, so those really are B0-only.

The pk8 gating is not settled. LCOMPILER-2841 reports that the nine
v_cvt_scale_pk8_* opcodes exist on A0 at identical encodings, that they
were originally block32-only, and that B0 added one extra OP_SEL bit
selecting block16 grouping on top. If that is confirmed, gating them here
is a pure loss: all 60 call sites in these headers pass scale_sel = 0,
which falls in A0's block32 range (0-3 for fp4, 0-7 for fp8/bf8), and the
software fallback costs roughly 9.5x the instruction count.

Introduce HIP_ENABLE_GFX1250_PK8_SCALE_BUILTINS and move the 23 pk8 sites
onto it - 8 in amd_hip_fp4.h and 15 in amd_hip_ocp_fp.hpp - leaving the 16
pk16 sites on HIP_ENABLE_GFX1250_BLOCK16_BUILTINS. The guards partition
cleanly: no site references both pk8 and pk16 builtins.

Once LCOMPILER-2841 lands, restoring hardware use of the pk8 converts is a
one-line change to this macro instead of an edit across 23 guards, and it
cannot accidentally re-enable the pk16 paths.

No functional change. Verified on both targets with a TU instantiating the
fp4/fp6/fp8 classes plus the non-scaled and all nine scaled OCP entry
points: gfx1250 emits 8 pk8 + 4 pk16 in 108 instructions, gfx1250-strict
emits 0 of each in 1024 - both identical to before this commit. Flipping
HIP_ENABLE_GFX1250_PK8_SCALE_BUILTINS to 1 makes gfx1250-strict attempt the
builtins again and fail against today's compiler, confirming the macro
controls exactly those sites.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 66be2922cd437416e34e3182b221c140bc60148c)
